WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.275 --> 00:00:02.678 line:10%
Hi, I'm Eli Roth
with Fandango MOVIECLIPS.

00:00:02.678 --> 00:00:05.903 line:10%
Here's some things to know before you
go for my new film <i>The Green Inferno</i>.

00:00:05.903 --> 00:00:06.913 line:90%
(SCREAMING)

00:00:08.369 --> 00:00:11.224 line:90%
<i>The Green Inferno </i>is about a bunch
of students from New York city that

00:00:11.224 --> 00:00:13.636 line:90%
decide they're going to go
and save the Amazon and they're going

00:00:13.636 --> 00:00:17.105 line:90%
to stop construction to protect
the last uncontacted tribe.

00:00:17.105 --> 00:00:20.035 line:90%
They save the tribe and on
the way home, their plane crashes

00:00:20.035 --> 00:00:21.718 line:90%
and the villagers think
they're intruders

00:00:21.718 --> 00:00:23.943 line:90%
and dart them and take them
to the village, and they--

00:00:23.943 --> 00:00:25.840 line:90%
Kids become their food supply.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.567 line:90%
<i>The Green Inferno </i>is filmed
in a village that is completely

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:29.786 line:90%
cut off from society.

00:00:29.786 --> 00:00:31.828 line:90%
We had to conceptually explain to

00:00:31.828 --> 00:00:33.342 line:90%
this village what a movie was.

00:00:33.342 --> 00:00:34.452 line:90%
How do we do that?

00:00:34.452 --> 00:00:36.740 line:90%
The Peruvian producers gathered
the whole village around and said

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.479 line:90%
we're gonna show you a movie
called <i>Cannibal Holocaust</i>.

00:00:39.479 --> 00:00:42.144 line:90%
This is the single most
violent film ever made.

00:00:42.144 --> 00:00:45.585 line:90%
Luckily, the village thought it was
a comedy, all 300 villagers voted and

00:00:45.585 --> 00:00:47.560 line:90%
they agreed to let us shoot there.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.041 line:90%
-(SHOUTING)
-(DRUMS BEATING)

00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:51.870 line:90%
Now, these people had
never acted before,

00:00:51.895 --> 00:00:55.499 line:90%
so we had to explain to them
action, cut. The kids loved it.

00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:57.994 line:90%
They loved picking up the parts
of the dead bodies.

00:00:57.994 --> 00:00:59.505 line:90%
Everybody wanted to be
covered in blood.

00:00:59.505 --> 00:01:01.744 line:90%
Everybody wanted to eat somebody.
They all thought it was hilarious.

00:01:01.744 --> 00:01:04.512 line:90%
They thought we were making a comedy,
and they were amazing actors.

00:01:04.512 --> 00:01:06.906 line:90%
Imagine someone with no awareness
of the camera,

00:01:06.906 --> 00:01:09.216 line:90%
no frame of reference for
what it's like to be photographed.

00:01:09.216 --> 00:01:10.182 line:90%
So, they were amazing.

00:01:10.182 --> 00:01:12.496 line:90%
They were some of the best actors
I've ever worked with.

00:01:13.969 --> 00:01:15.973 line:90%
The kids in the movie really,
really got into it.

00:01:15.973 --> 00:01:19.025 line:90%
They caught a baby python.
They thought it'd be funny if when

00:01:19.025 --> 00:01:21.920 line:90%
the Americans were in the cage,
you threw a live snake at them.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.000 line:90%
That's actually a great idea!

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.804 line:90%
We were shooting in Chile where the
safety laws are a little different

00:01:25.804 --> 00:01:27.765 line:90%
the actors, Kirby and Magda,
looked at me and go,

00:01:27.765 --> 00:01:29.109 line:90%
"Wait, is that thing poisonous?"

00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:30.692 line:90%
We go "No, no, no, it's a python,
don't worry."

00:01:30.692 --> 00:01:33.576 line:90%
I'm hiding behind the camera
and go "Action! <i>Acción</i>!" and the kids

00:01:33.576 --> 00:01:36.992 line:90%
are just like dangling, slapping
these girls in the face with

00:01:36.992 --> 00:01:40.477 line:90%
a python and if you freeze frame it,
the snake is like--

00:01:40.477 --> 00:01:41.559 line:90%
(HISSING)

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:44.860 line:90%
And its teeth are out literally
an inch from their eyeballs.

00:01:45.302 --> 00:01:47.626 line:90%
<i>The Green Inferno </i>is inspired by
Occupy Wall Street.

00:01:47.626 --> 00:01:50.079 line:90%
It's about kids that latch on
to causes that they don't know

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:53.030 line:90%
everything about or don't believe in
or latch onto it because it's trendy.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.093 line:90%
I kept noticing hashtag of the week.
It's everyone going

00:01:56.093 --> 00:01:57.294 line:90%
"How can you not care!"

00:01:57.294 --> 00:01:59.355 line:90%
Kony 2012, Child Soldiers in Uganda.

00:01:59.355 --> 00:02:03.263 line:90%
You get the feeling that now there
are these social justice warriors

00:02:03.263 --> 00:02:05.761 line:90%
out there to make you feel bad
about everything.

00:02:05.761 --> 00:02:07.321 line:90%
Social activism can be great.

00:02:07.321 --> 00:02:09.155 line:90%
It can be this amazing
vehicle for change,

00:02:09.155 --> 00:02:12.262 line:90%
but so many people, I feel, doing it
not because they believe

00:02:12.262 --> 00:02:14.269 line:90%
in the cause, but want
to look like they care.

00:02:14.269 --> 00:02:15.980 line:90%
They love being on
the home page of Reddit.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.941 line:90%
I want to see kids like that
just get eaten, eyeballs torn out,

00:02:18.941 --> 00:02:21.323 line:90%
get their tongues sliced off,
genitals mutilated.

00:02:21.323 --> 00:02:24.678 line:90%
I want full-on cannibal gore.

00:02:24.678 --> 00:02:25.893 line:90%
That for me is hilarious.

00:02:25.893 --> 00:02:28.602 line:90%
So, <i>Green Inferno </i>is
a terrifying movie,

00:02:28.602 --> 00:02:30.077 line:90%
but in a very perverse way,

00:02:30.077 --> 00:02:31.841 line:90%
it's fun to watch
these kids get it.

00:02:31.841 --> 00:02:33.492 line:90%
(SCREAMING)

00:02:33.492 --> 00:02:35.809 line:90%
I'm Eli Roth
for Fandango MOVIECLIPS.

00:02:35.809 --> 00:02:37.876 line:90%
Thanks for watching
and check out <i>The Green Inferno</i>.

00:02:37.876 --> 00:02:40.349 line:90%
September 25th.
Can you take the heat?

